  "title": "Weekly Metasploit Update: Modules for Audiobookshelf, LiteLLM, Next.js, Dalfox and more",
  "summary": "Metasploit is currently seeking user feedback on planned improvements to evasion capabilities via a proposal and feedback form that remains open until July 1, 2026. The latest update includes several new security modules, such as detection scanners for Audiobookshelf, LiteLLM Proxy, and Next.js, along with a new exploit module for Dalfox. Additionally, the release incorporates improvements to authentication brute-force modules and networking sockets, with further details and documentation available on the official Metasploit docsite.",
